---
args: { input: CaseInput }
returns: RunProposal
---
1. Bind `goal = await frameRequest(input)` from the request and `policy = await selectPolicy(input)` from supplied authority candidates. Preserve unresolved precedence instead of guessing which source governs.
2. Bind `work = await formTaskGraph(goal)` and `evidencePlan = await planEvidence(input, work)` so each operation has explicit prerequisites and a searched source universe.
3. Run the stages in their dependency order. The first stage receives only `input.domainRecords.firstStage`; every later stage receives the preceding function's actual accepted records. Bind each full result separately.
const extractPromisesResult = await extractPromises(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan);
const probeBehaviorResult = await probeBehavior(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan, extractPromisesResult.accepted);
const classifyMismatchResult = await classifyMismatch(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan, probeBehaviorResult.accepted);
const constructRepairsResult = await constructRepairs(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan, classifyMismatchResult.accepted);
const verifyConsistencyResult = await verifyConsistency(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan, constructRepairsResult.accepted);
4. Bind `stageSet: CaseStageSet = { extractPromises: extractPromisesResult, probeBehavior: probeBehaviorResult, classifyMismatch: classifyMismatchResult, constructRepairs: constructRepairsResult, verifyConsistency: verifyConsistencyResult }` and `collection: CollectionFinding = await reconcileCollection(stageSet)`. Bind `allQuestions: string[] = [...extractPromisesResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...probeBehaviorResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...classifyMismatchResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...constructRepairsResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...verifyConsistencyResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...collection.coverageGaps]` and `questions: QuestionBatch = await resolveQuestions(allQuestions, input)`.
5. Bind `invalidation = await assessDelta(input)`, `review = await prepareReview(collection)`, and `view = await composeView(review, input)`; pass each child its actual declared inputs and retain the returned object.
6. Bind `allChecks: CheckResult[] = [...extractPromisesResult.checks, ...probeBehaviorResult.checks, ...classifyMismatchResult.checks, ...constructRepairsResult.checks, ...verifyConsistencyResult.checks]`. Bind `hasGateFailure = allChecks.some(check => check.verdict !== "pass")` and `hasBlocker = input.authorityStatus !== "authorized" || questions.questions.length > 0 || collection.coverageGaps.length > 0`. Bind `disposition: "proposed" | "blocked" | "needs-review" = hasBlocker ? "blocked" : hasGateFailure ? "needs-review" : "proposed"`. Bind `rationale: string[] = allChecks.map(check => `${check.check}: ${check.verdict}; evidence ${check.evidenceIds.join(",")}`)`.
7. Operational detail 1 — An example depends on a deprecated service: mark its environment and provide a reviewed replacement. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (mark its environment and provide a reviewed replacement.) through the existing stage result for DocumentedPromise; preserve exact source/version and the prior DocumentedPromise, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
8. Operational detail 2 — A translated page lags the source: track edition mismatch separately from mistranslation. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (track edition mismatch separately from mistranslation.) through the existing stage result for DocumentedPromise; preserve exact source/version and the prior DocumentedPromise, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
9. Operational detail 3 — A behavior bug is fixed later: retain the earlier documentation decision in history. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (retain the earlier documentation decision in history.) through the existing stage result for DocumentedPromise; preserve exact source/version and the prior DocumentedPromise, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
10. Operational detail 4 — A code sample includes a secret: block export and rotate any exposed credential through operations. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (block export and rotate any exposed credential through operations.) through the existing stage result for DocumentedPromise; preserve exact source/version and the prior DocumentedPromise, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
11. Operational detail 5 — A page is edited during review: rebase and revalidate changed claims. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (rebase and revalidate changed claims.) through the existing stage result for DocumentedPromise; preserve exact source/version and the prior DocumentedPromise, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
12. Initialize `revisions: RevisionProposal[] = []`. If any gate is not pass, bind `revision = await proposeRevision(the failed check names, the smallest affected stage name)` and add that returned proposal to revisions. Bind and return `result: RunProposal = { caseId: input.caseId, goal, policy, work, evidencePlan, extractPromises: extractPromisesResult, probeBehavior: probeBehaviorResult, classifyMismatch: classifyMismatchResult, constructRepairs: constructRepairsResult, verifyConsistency: verifyConsistencyResult, collection, questions, invalidation, review, view, revisions, disposition, rationale }`. Proposed actions remain proposals. The host owns authorization, persistence, effect dispatch and verification.
